  "content": {
    "id": "p28-q16-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "16",
    "prompt": "Count non-negative integers, including $0$. A one-digit integer satisfies either ordering condition.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p28-q16a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "How many integers (of any size) have digits in strictly increasing order (reading from left to right)?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$512$.\n\nEach non-empty subset of $\\{1,2,\\ldots,9\\}$ gives one increasing integer; also count $0$.",
          "worked": "Zero cannot occur in a multi-digit increasing integer, since it would be the leading digit. Each non-empty subset of $\\{1,2,\\ldots,9\\}$ gives exactly one integer when its digits are written in increasing order. Include the single-digit integer $0$ separately.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}N&=(2^9-1)+1\\\\N&=512.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p28-q16b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "How many integers (of any size) have digits in strictly decreasing order (reading from left to right)?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$1023$.\n\nEach non-empty subset of the ten digits gives exactly one decreasing integer.",
          "worked": "Each non-empty subset of $\\{0,1,\\ldots,9\\}$ gives exactly one integer when its digits are written in decreasing order. Any selected zero is last, so there is no leading zero; the subset $\\{0\\}$ gives the integer $0$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}N&=2^{10}-1\\\\N&=1023.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 25
      }
    ]
  },
